  |title Joseph as a father — de-escalating rather than matching the anger

  |summary
    Suzanna's own account of Joseph responding to her son's anger by talking him
    through his emotions rather than reacting to the disrespect in how it was
    delivered, told directly to an agent as an example of who Joseph is.

  |account
    Here is a real life example of Joseph as a father to one of my kids: Just the
    other night, my son was very angry and frustrated. My son yelled at me and
    ordered me to come fix his problem. It upset me that he was being unkind.
    Joseph very lovingly and patiently talked with my son about his emotions and
    helped him to de-escalate, priming him for a meaningful conversation and a
    bonding moment with me. It had been a long time since my son had hugged me in
    a long embrace. My son apologised to me and grew more mature and kind because
    of that moment.

  |what-would-have-happened-instead
    Suzanna's framing names her own reaction as the live alternative: she was
    upset by the unkindness in the moment. Matching that — responding to the
    disrespect in how the request was made rather than to the emotion underneath
    it — was the available default and is what she describes herself as feeling
    pulled toward. The account's whole point is that Joseph did the other thing:
    addressed the emotion first, which is what made the apology and the embrace
    possible afterward rather than a prolonged conflict about tone.

  |provenance
    Secondhand — Suzanna's own account, told in her own words directly to an
    agent (not reconstructed by the agent from a transcript of the event itself,
    since the event had no agent present). This is the corpus's first segment
    whose speaker is Suzanna rather than Joseph; kept because a testimony about
    Joseph, from someone with the closest possible vantage, is exactly the kind
    of account this corpus's third directory exists for, per the README's
    argument that a narrative can transmit what a precept cannot.

  |working-notes
    No `:demonstrates` target exists yet in vera/ for the virtue this shows
    (something like "address the emotion under a disrespectful delivery rather
    than the delivery itself") — the field above is a plain label, not a live
    reference, until such a segment exists.
